# Profile: medium. An 8 GB Docker VM. Only the scheduler container is raised,
# because it hosts the Spark driver and was the one service that hit its ceiling
# in the 6 GB runs (docs/benchmarks.md), and ClickHouse, whose 1.13 GiB server
# limit (90% of the old 1280m ceiling) rejected the 1M-row load. Ceilings sum to
# about 8.3 GiB, above an 8 GB VM, on purpose: Spark has finished before the
# warehouse load starts, so the two peaks do not coincide.
#
# Applied to .env by `make profile PROFILE=medium`.
MEM_KAFKA=768m
MEM_KAFKA_HEAP="-Xmx384m -Xms384m"
MEM_POSTGRES=320m
MEM_CLICKHOUSE=2048m
MEM_REDIS=48m
MEM_S3=1024m
S3_GOMEMLIMIT=768MiB
MEM_AIRFLOW_APISERVER=448m
MEM_AIRFLOW_SCHEDULER=3328m
MEM_AIRFLOW_DAGPROC=384m
MEM_OPS=128m
SPARK_DRIVER_MEMORY=2g
SPARK_SHUFFLE_PARTITIONS=16
GEN_EVENT_COUNT=50000
